ere in space  any motion of the rock will activate the  Coriolis effect that effect makes the  path of the rocks spiral back into l4 or  l5 in our analogy it's as if the motion  of the ball changes the mountain which  sounds a little strange but rotating  frames are weird like that anyway I've  only been using the moon's orbit so I  could draw things to scale the most  useful Lagrange's points are actually on  Earth's orbit around the Sun if you want  a space probe to monitor the Sun we put  it in l1 like Soho if you want it to  always point away from the Sun you put  it at l2 like plunk unfortunately bills  require course corrections every month  or so l3 lasts a bit longer but it's not  much used since it's always blocked by  the Sun it could never send us  information l4 and l5 are so stable they  tend to collect space junk naturally  they don't even need to be related to  the earth  orbit's have these points my favorites  are l4 and l5 for Jupiter they're filled  to the brim with asteroids so what are  the grudge points there are five special  points around the orbit of a planet or  moon they orbit with the planet or moon  so their locations of stability objects  can remain stationary with respect to  the planet remove some of them are fully  stable while others are only semi stable  but the two least stable points are  actually the most useful we regularly  put space probes there for a consistent  view of the universe so what do you  think about lagrangian's  cool not cool let us know in the  comments thanks for liking and sharing  this video don't forget to subscribe if  you'd like to keep up with us and until  next time remember it's okay to be a  little crazy we all have our everyday  grooming routines from showering to  brushing our teeth - yes  shaving I don't know about you but I  shower and brush my teeth every day no  matter your routine Dollar Shave Club  has everything you need to help you look  feel and smell your best a lot of you've  probably heard